{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JbMGe75VGPEUTJWpXUmzoW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have the file. Now let me extract the specific requirements you asked for.\n\n## R3.1 - R3.3 (Already Implemented)\n\n**R3.1:** Must support --color=always, --color=auto, and --color=never. When --color is given without a value, it must default to \"always\".\n\n**R3.2:** --color=auto must colorize output only when stdout is a TTY. Uses pkg/sys.IsTerminal(os.Stdout) for detection. When stdout is not a TTY, --color=auto behaves like --color=never.\n\n**R3.3:** Colorized output uses GNU LS_COLORS default color assignments via pkg/format. Calls pkg/format.FileTypeColor(mode os.FileMode) string for ANSI codes and pkg/format.Reset() for reset sequence. Executable detection: fi.Mode&0o111 != 0. Each entry name is wrapped with color codes. The process-global color mode is set via pkg/format.SetColorEnabled(true/false). When disabled, FileTypeColor returns empty strings.\n\n## R3.4 - R3.7 (Requested Requirements)\n\n**R3.4:**\n- **Text:** When --color=never or when color is suppressed (non-TTY with auto), must not emit any ANSI escape sequences in the output.\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** AC4 traces this requirement.\n\n**R3.5:**\n- **Text:** -h must only take effect with -l (long format). When -h is given with -l, file sizes (fi.Size int64) must be displayed via pkg/format.HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string with opts.Binary = true (1024-base units, suffixes K/M/G/T/P/E). Without -l, -h must have no visible effect on output.\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** AC5 traces this requirement (along with many R1 requirements).\n\n**R3.6:**\n- **Text:** -h must also apply to the \"total N\" block count line in long format. When -h is active, convert the total block count (sum(fi.Blocks)/2 as int64) to a human-readable string using the same binary algorithm before printing \"total X\\n\".\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** AC5 traces this requirement.\n\n**R3.7:**\n- **Text:** -h must apply to -s block counts when both -s and -h are given, converting block counts to human-readable form. Use pkg/format.HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string with opts.Binary = true, consistent with R3.5. Do not duplicate the HumanSize algorithm inline.\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** AC14 traces this requirement.\n\nAll four requirements (R3.4-R3.7) have no explicit non-goals sections - their scope is simply defined by their requirement text and acceptance criteria."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc084725-cea8-4998-8eed-e375644451ce","uuid":"3985d157-397b-4a6d-9a80-3f0a7c512972","timestamp":"2026-05-14T22:20:00.465Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the file docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml in /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5220. I need to see requirements R3.4, R3.5, R3.6, and R3.7 specifically. Search for these requirement IDs in the file and give me their full text including acceptance criteria and any non_goals. Also tell me what R3.1-R3.3 say briefly so I understand what was already implemented.","agentId":"a3e77f017fdf55086","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have the file. Now let me extract the specific requirements you asked for.\n\n## R3.1 - R3.3 (Already Implemented)\n\n**R3.1:** Must support --color=always, --color=auto, and --color=never. When --color is given without a value, it must default to \"always\".\n\n**R3.2:** --color=auto must colorize output only when stdout is a TTY. Uses pkg/sys.IsTerminal(os.Stdout) for detection. When stdout is not a TTY, --color=auto behaves like --color=never.\n\n**R3.3:** Colorized output uses GNU LS_COLORS default color assignments via pkg/format. Calls pkg/format.FileTypeColor(mode os.FileMode) string for ANSI codes and pkg/format.Reset() for reset sequence. Executable detection: fi.Mode&0o111 != 0. Each entry name is wrapped with color codes. The process-global color mode is set via pkg/format.SetColorEnabled(true/false). When disabled, FileTypeColor returns empty strings.\n\n## R3.4 - R3.7 (Requested Requirements)\n\n**R3.4:**\n- **Text:** When --color=never or when color is suppressed (non-TTY with auto), must not emit any ANSI escape sequences in the output.\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** AC4 traces this requirement.\n\n**R3.5:**\n- **Text:** -h must only take effect with -l (long format). When -h is given with -l, file sizes (fi.Size int64) must be displayed via pkg/format.HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string with opts.Binary = true (1024-base units, suffixes K/M/G/T/P/E). Without -l, -h must have no visible effect on output.\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** AC5 traces this requirement (along with many R1 requirements).\n\n**R3.6:**\n- **Text:** -h must also apply to the \"total N\" block count line in long format. When -h is active, convert the total block count (sum(fi.Blocks)/2 as int64) to a human-readable string using the same binary algorithm before printing \"total X\\n\".\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** AC5 traces this requirement.\n\n**R3.7:**\n- **Text:** -h must apply to -s block counts when both -s and -h are given, converting block counts to human-readable form. Use pkg/format.HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string with opts.Binary = true, consistent with R3.5. Do not duplicate the HumanSize algorithm inline.\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** AC14 traces this requirement.\n\nAll four requirements (R3.4-R3.7) have no explicit non-goals sections - their scope is simply defined by their requirement text and acceptance criteria."}],"totalDurationMs":10788,"totalTokens":26663,"totalToolUseCount":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9824,"cache_read_input_tokens":16139,"output_tokens":695,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"epheme